# promise: #424
# With the sidebar hidden, a double-click on a tab in the sidebar that slides out at the window's
# edge opens the rename field with the keyboard in it. That sidebar is a panel that only becomes key
# when a click needs it; a click on a row doesn't, so the field showed its name selected while the
# keys went on to the window and its page, and the tab kept its old name.
requires screen
# Cra has to come to the front to have a key window; a background test copy never does.
env CRA_TEST_BACKGROUND=0
budget rss=800 stalls50=20
pace 0.4
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=pinned
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://action/pinTab
wait 1
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 0.5
cra://debug?activate=1
wait 1
cra://debug?keys=page
expect-log keys page: window,
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=hold
wait 1
cra://debug?snapshot=TabRowView&out=/dev/null
expect-log snapshot: TabRowView at \d+,\d+ size \d+x40
cra://debug?clickAt=150,254&clicks=2&target=floating
expect-log sidebar double-click: rename
wait 0.5
cra://debug?keys=rename
expect-log keys rename: floating sidebar, to NSTextView
# Still editing: the field didn't end on its own and save the old name.
reject-log sidebar rename:
cra://debug?checkStore=1
